### FINDING 2 — NONFATAL — location: Remarks, bullet 2
CLAIM AS WRITTEN: "The area under the spike does tend to $0$, which is why this example is also the standard warning that pointwise convergence controls no integral either."
WHY IT FAILS: as written this reads as a non sequitur: since the constructed spike has fixed height $1$, its area $= a_k \to 0$, so $\int f_k \to 0 = \int \mathbf{0}$ — the integral limit here is actually *correct*, so this specific witness does **not** demonstrate failure of $\int f_k \to \int f$. (The standard integral counterexample instead blows the height up, e.g. height $1/a_k$, to keep the area constant.) The very next clause, "Nothing about integration is claimed here," partially disclaims the sentence, leaving it self-qualifying rather than a clean false theorem.
WHAT WOULD FIX IT: reword to something like "unlike the height-scaled variant of this construction (used elsewhere to show integrals need not converge), the area here vanishes, so this witness makes no claim about integrals" — but given the immediate disclaimer already present, a careful reader is not actually misled within the 30-second window.

